#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "da92ef6c-cb0b-5a4c-9a0d-0f0a9db19616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4403" :question/problem "Let\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/5357fcb0ec150699b4d50cbd6fa9651c421ac3500660703396146362160328a2.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/63d354773d145f05e73e808efe2a21164cb28d6ff19ae104d6bbde6510cf10e6.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "c677ee1a-d3c2-534c-985c-efaa5dc04c86" :question/math-academy-id "e-4404" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $AB$?" :question/worked-solution "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "9352349d-64e0-5437-9d72-7e7f7e571064" :question/math-academy-id "e-4405" :question/problem "Let\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/035755bae569c8c9323112891f959076dd727d3ef40ba66c6c40dadf5ddc8f84.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/e53c9ba3bb64b81e44f8f4f49ac77408b7db6ee458be3d43b687d9ed8897ad59.png)\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008c1879-9556-51a5-a9dc-077c78496cf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282843} {:answer/id #uuid "096cdb96-9de6-58c7-8667-5c74ea9b3486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282844} {:answer/id #uuid "d7112520-a7ff-51c0-afbb-d5d0014f08ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282845} {:answer/id #uuid "6f646e8b-6f9f-50fe-b6b7-64a7f9150698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\times 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282846} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fab64e-ade5-511b-8db1-15982f19c761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "008c1879-9556-51a5-a9dc-077c78496cf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282843} :answer-field/id #uuid "473e9f83-5629-5fb4-9aa1-00506e9689c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8b515a2-1e51-5386-9e18-dbb3647fc2cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-129486" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $8\\times 7$ matrix and $B$ is a  $2\\times 8$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "There are $8$ columns in $B$ and $8$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication, and $BA$ is a $2\\times 7$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{8}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{8}}\\times 7}={BA}_{2\\times 7}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83ac9905-b3d3-5121-a0af-d8d82ac98cf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319928} {:answer/id #uuid "754569d8-841e-5f10-85f5-f157644a1661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319929} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d93bad-fcc3-5732-9a35-6b1f87e389be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319930} {:answer/id #uuid "d66cd3fb-68ef-5e9f-8738-c4ecb686ba8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319931} {:answer/id #uuid "8e31435a-3348-5fd6-a47f-3b01176c93d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d66cd3fb-68ef-5e9f-8738-c4ecb686ba8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319931} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c53eec0-77cb-51af-871b-575a15bbc493" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "960a6f14-6ea1-5d58-9c80-cf93ecc61484" :question/math-academy-id "q-22056" :question/problem "$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $R,S,$ and $T?$\n\n- The product $SR$ is well defined\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $ST$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $T$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $T.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $T,$ the matrices $S$ and $T$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90716581-7657-5710-a416-0a4ec699aa36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099148} {:answer/id #uuid "b716eea0-edd5-58bb-b055-75db0e36beff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099149} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6a988a-1034-5b6d-8874-27744a0316a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099150} {:answer/id #uuid "6809684d-a629-5f4a-88b6-28baf9fb78bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099151} {:answer/id #uuid "6d697e18-fa26-5eff-83d2-34701c398525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90716581-7657-5710-a416-0a4ec699aa36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099148} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc161804-7baa-5167-a58b-36129a2a7040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9258b6d8-3a2c-54d4-bc2f-8b9ea4ccd825" :question/math-academy-id "q-22063" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\n- The product $AB$ is well defined\n- The product $BA$ is well defined\n- The product $AC$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{3\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d28e41c1-21c4-5ee3-9aba-5f37e9739594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319934} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd2ca00-02a5-551f-83aa-847ec5fb3811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319935} {:answer/id #uuid "2c2f1a92-0a50-5200-9d19-30cc59dafed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319936} {:answer/id #uuid "2f735c2e-62cb-5008-a066-afcaf727c043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319937} {:answer/id #uuid "87f89560-fa29-5d56-a82d-349cd46d4c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d28e41c1-21c4-5ee3-9aba-5f37e9739594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319934} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2f6a893-9c8a-5b2a-bd80-f9bb911d3711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a867edc2-7d3a-5fbc-b2ed-43a1f2230791" :question/math-academy-id "q-22067" :question/problem "Let\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd238fd9-001b-5b3f-954f-b174c4b76d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd238fd9-001b-5b3f-954f-b174c4b76d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319941} :answer-field/id #uuid "97874cca-b9ad-579a-b527-d4073c9a22f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f3dc238-670c-5ed2-ae5d-0e49ad69c709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f3dc238-670c-5ed2-ae5d-0e49ad69c709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319943} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ed2ebca-af91-5e81-9d54-244a860a3893" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5e338965-f7d6-5609-93d3-3bc22e98244b" :question/math-academy-id "q-275395" :question/problem "Let\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -5 \\\\ 11 & 13\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThen, the dimensions of $BA$ are{{field-1}}$\\times $\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7aadff4-b2fe-5b67-9a70-b428529790b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319946} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd7f911-4e80-5f33-bb42-302e2cdb931c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dd7f911-4e80-5f33-bb42-302e2cdb931c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319947} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f4a484-c4e3-530b-bd77-32864dad5c76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer